  "title": "A better place to try the whole stack",
  "summary": "June made Pollinations easier to explore, easier to build on, and more rewarding to contribute to across every modality.\n\nA standalone React Playground brought image, video, text, and audio models into one testing space, while the SDK, UI kit, live model catalog, CDN bundle, and EmbedBridge made those capabilities easier to bring into other apps.\n\nClaude Fable 5 and Sonnet 5, Kimi K2.7 Code, MiniMax M3, GLM-5.2, Qwen3.7 Plus, Ideogram 4.0, Mercury 2, and Nano Banana 2 Lite joined or upgraded the roster, alongside sharper 1080p video options.\n\nElevenLabs gained sound effects, multilingual TTS, reference-conditioned music, and longer inputs, while Stable Audio 3 added long-form stereo generation and audio-to-audio style transfer.\n\nQuests moved from a dashboard preview to a live rewards ledger: people can complete useful actions, claim Pollen, follow activity on a scoreboard, earn for listing apps, and inspect rewards from the polli CLI.",
